{"sidebar": "<div class=\"toc-sidebar\"><div class=\"sidebar-header toc-sidebar-header\"><button class=\"sidebar-close\" title=\"Close\" aria-label=\"Close table of contents\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"1em\" height=\"1em\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.25\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-x bn-icon bn-icon-close\" focusable=\"false\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" d=\"M18 6 6 18\"></path><path vector-effect=\"non-scaling-stroke\" d=\"m6 6 12 12\"></path></svg></button></div><div class=\"toc-sidebar-body\"><nav class=\"v2-nav\" aria-label=\"Codebooks\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-nav\"><div class=\"toc-heading\">Default auto-tags</div><a href=\"#\" class=\"toc-link codebook-toc-link v2-nav-row\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-nav-row-sentiment\"><span class=\"v2-nav-text\"><span class=\"codebook-toc-label\">Emotional &amp; Cognitive Signals</span></span><span class=\"sw mini \" role=\"switch\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-checked=\"true\" aria-label=\"Emotional &amp; Cognitive Signals\"></span></a><a href=\"#\" class=\"toc-link codebook-toc-link v2-nav-row active\" aria-current=\"location\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-nav-row-uxr\"><span class=\"v2-nav-text\"><span class=\"codebook-toc-label\">Bristlenose UXR Codebook</span></span><span class=\"v2-nav-pending\">9</span><span class=\"sw mini \" role=\"switch\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-checked=\"true\" aria-label=\"Bristlenose UXR Codebook\"></span></a><div class=\"toc-heading\">Manual tags</div><a href=\"#\" class=\"toc-link codebook-toc-link v2-nav-row\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-nav-row-floor\"><span class=\"v2-nav-text\"><span class=\"codebook-toc-label\">Project ‘Demo study’ tags</span></span></a><div class=\"toc-heading\">Frameworks</div><a href=\"#\" class=\"toc-link codebook-toc-link v2-nav-row\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-nav-row-yablonski\"><span class=\"v2-nav-text\"><span class=\"codebook-toc-label\">Laws of UX</span><span class=\"v2-nav-provenance\">Jon Yablonski</span></span><span class=\"v2-nav-pending\">5</span><span class=\"sw mini \" role=\"switch\" tabindex=\"0\" aria-checked=\"true\" aria-label=\"Laws of UX\"></span></a><button type=\"button\" class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-secondary bn-btn-sm\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-nav-browse\">Browse Codebooks</button></nav></div><div class=\"drag-handle toc-drag-handle\" role=\"separator\" aria-orientation=\"vertical\" aria-valuenow=\"240\" aria-valuemin=\"200\" aria-valuemax=\"480\" aria-label=\"Resize table of contents\" tabindex=\"0\"></div></div>", "section": "<section data-testid=\"bn-codebook-v2\"><div class=\"section-heading\"><h1>Codebooks</h1><div class=\"section-heading-action\"><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-secondary bn-btn-lg\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-browse\">Browse Codebooks</button></div></div><div class=\"v2-layout\"><div class=\"v2-main\"><div data-testid=\"bn-v2-browse-grid\"><div class=\"v2-card-grid\"><div class=\"picker-card\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-sentiment\"><div class=\"picker-card-title\">Emotional &amp; Cognitive Signals</div><div class=\"picker-card-author prov-system\">On by default</div><div class=\"picker-card-desc\">Seven sentiment categories designed for UX research.</div><div class=\"picker-card-footrow\"><span class=\"picker-card-status\">7 tags · applied to 18 quotes in Demo study</span></div></div><div class=\"picker-card\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-uxr\"><div class=\"picker-card-title\">Bristlenose UXR Codebook</div><div class=\"picker-card-author prov-system\">Available by default</div><div class=\"picker-card-desc\">A practitioner-oriented codebook for any user research study.</div><div class=\"picker-card-footrow\"><span class=\"picker-card-status\">34 tags · applied to 10 quotes in Demo study</span><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-secondary picker-card-toggle picker-card-toggle-uninstall\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-action-uxr\">Uninstall</button></div></div><div class=\"picker-card\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-cli-ux\"><div class=\"picker-card-title\">Command-Line UX</div><div class=\"picker-card-author prov-system\">Available by default</div><div class=\"picker-card-desc\">Tags for research on command-line tools, developer tools, and sysadmin workflows — anywhere the primary interface is a terminal.</div><div class=\"picker-card-footrow\"><span class=\"picker-card-status\">35 tags</span><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-primary picker-card-toggle\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-action-cli-ux\">Install</button></div></div><div class=\"picker-card\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-garrett\"><div class=\"picker-card-title\">The Elements of User Experience</div><div class=\"picker-card-author\">Jesse James Garrett</div><div class=\"picker-card-desc\">Five planes of user experience, from abstract to concrete — strategy, scope, structure, skeleton, surface — each dependent on the plane below it, and each with two sides: the product as functionality and the product as information.</div><div class=\"picker-card-footrow\"><span class=\"picker-card-status\">18 tags</span><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-primary picker-card-toggle\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-action-garrett\">Install</button></div></div><div class=\"picker-card\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-morville\"><div class=\"picker-card-title\">The User Experience Honeycomb</div><div class=\"picker-card-author\">Peter Morville</div><div class=\"picker-card-desc\">Seven facets of user experience — useful, usable, desirable, findable, accessible, credible, valuable — drawn as a honeycomb so that each can be \"a singular looking glass\" on a product.</div><div class=\"picker-card-footrow\"><span class=\"picker-card-status\">15 tags</span><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-primary picker-card-toggle\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-action-morville\">Install</button></div></div><div class=\"picker-card\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-nielsen\"><div class=\"picker-card-title\">10 Usability Heuristics for User Interface Design</div><div class=\"picker-card-author\">Jakob Nielsen</div><div class=\"picker-card-desc\">Ten broad rules of thumb for interaction design, refined from a factor analysis of 249 usability problems.</div><div class=\"picker-card-footrow\"><span class=\"picker-card-status\">34 tags</span><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-primary picker-card-toggle\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-action-nielsen\">Install</button></div></div><div class=\"picker-card\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-norman\"><div class=\"picker-card-title\">The Design of Everyday Things</div><div class=\"picker-card-author\">Don Norman</div><div class=\"picker-card-desc\">Norman's seven fundamental principles of design — discoverability, feedback, conceptual model, affordances, signifiers, mappings and constraints — plus his classification of human error into slips and mistakes.</div><div class=\"picker-card-footrow\"><span class=\"picker-card-status\">28 tags</span><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-primary picker-card-toggle\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-action-norman\">Install</button></div></div><div class=\"picker-card\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-yablonski\"><div class=\"picker-card-title\">Laws of UX</div><div class=\"picker-card-author\">Jon Yablonski</div><div class=\"picker-card-desc\">A collection of psychological principles that underpin user experience, drawn from cognitive psychology, perception science, and behavioural economics.</div><div class=\"picker-card-footrow\"><span class=\"picker-card-status\">24 tags · applied to 3 quotes in Demo study</span><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-secondary picker-card-toggle picker-card-toggle-uninstall\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-action-yablonski\">Uninstall</button></div></div><div class=\"picker-card\" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-plato\"><div class=\"picker-card-title\">Platonic Ontology &amp; Epistemology</div><div class=\"picker-card-author\">Composite — Vlastos, Fine, Kraut, Sedley</div><div class=\"picker-card-desc\">A scholarly codebook for analysing Plato's dialogues through the lens of his ontology (Theory of Forms, cosmology, soul) and epistemology (knowledge vs opinion, dialectic, recollection).</div><div class=\"picker-card-footrow\"><span class=\"picker-card-status\">26 tags</span><button class=\"bn-btn bn-btn-primary picker-card-toggle\" data-testid=\"bn-v2-card-action-plato\">Install</button></div></div></div></div></div></div></section>", "sidebarWidth": 240, "mainWidth": 892, "sectionWidth": 892}